# Agente de impressão (fonte oficial)

This is the official local print-agent architecture. Deploys, refactors, and new features must not replace it.

1. Coverage of printing = local agent on the **store PC** at `http://127.0.0.1:19191`. The Vercel site cannot print silently by itself.
2. Autostart = Windows watchdog via `tools/burger-gn-print-agent/install-autostart.bat` (copy under `%LOCALAPPDATA%\BurgerGN\print-agent`, ONLOGON task, Startup `startup-logon.vbs`, protocol `burgergn-print://`). Registration is file copy + `schtasks.exe` — never PowerShell / `.ps1` / `CreateShortcut` (Avast IDP.ALEXA.54 and similar heuristics). Seed/migration/deploy of the website must not remove this. The installer is the only one-time setup on the store PC.
3. Runtime must be **headless**: launch only via `wscript.exe` + `start-hidden.vbs` (`WshShell.Run` window style 0). Never use `cmd.exe`, `.bat`, `.cmd`, or `.ps1` as the scheduled-task / protocol / Startup action — those open a black console or get quarantined. Logs go to `agent.log` only, not a console window. `watchdog.mjs` spawns the server with `windowsHide: true`.
4. If the agent process dies, `watchdog.mjs` restarts it. The admin UI polls `/health`, auto-wakes via `burgergn-print://start`, and exposes **Reconectar Impressora** (`reconnectPrintAgent`). Do not ship an offline state that only says "Agente offline".
5. User-facing copy when the agent is really down must tell them to click **Reconectar Impressora**, then run `install-autostart.bat` **once** on the store PC if it still fails. Do not tell staff to open `start.bat` on every use.
6. `silentPrintOrder` / `silentPrintTest` must call `ensurePrintAgent` before giving up. `PrintAgentGuard` stays on every protected admin route.
7. Do not delete the installer, watchdog, protocol handler, or reconnect button in future deploys.

Keep `scripts/test-print-agent-keepalive.mjs` and `scripts/test-silent-print-agent.mjs` passing.
